WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.460
Deployment controls turn trust decisions into enforceable operating behavior.

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.480
A model that passed intake should not become a vague recommendation.

3
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:17.260
It should become a specific approved artifact, version, registry reference, deployment configuration, and rollback option.

4
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:24.900
Production or shared environments should use approved model versions, not whatever file happens to be available locally.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.680
Version pinning, artifact registries, access controls, promotion gates, and deployment approvals reduce accidental or unauthorized model changes.

6
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:38.780
They also make it easier to explain what changed when behavior shifts.

7
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.940
Environment separation helps keep experiments from quietly becoming dependencies.

8
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:50.200
Research and staging environments can move faster, but production paths should require clearer evidence.

9
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:59.980
A checkpoint that is useful for exploration may still need license review, evaluation, integrity checks, and owner approval before it supports shared workflows.

10
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:06.340
Runtime governance should preserve useful observability without collecting too much sensitive data.

11
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:17.880
Logs should identify model version, deployment context, request path, and operational status while avoiding unnecessary prompt, output, or protected data retention.

12
00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:21.580
Access to logs should match the sensitivity of the workflow.

13
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:29.620
Rollback plans matter because even approved model changes can create quality, compatibility, performance, or policy issues.

14
00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:38.200
A governed deployment can promote, monitor, pause, and revert model versions without scrambling to reconstruct what happened from local files and memory.

15
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:41.280
Governance also needs routine drift checks.

16
00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:49.460
Deployment automation should detect when a running environment no longer matches the approved registry reference, configuration, or version pin.

17
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:57.560
That makes checkpoint substitution, accidental local edits, and unmanaged hot fixes easier to catch before they become normal practice.
